  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="4.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIIAtr">VII Atr</ref> 4.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4.1" corresp="#wit-q">Et omnis consuetudo reddatur super amicitiam Dei ad matrem ecclesiam, cui adiacet.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="4.1" corresp="#wit-q">Et omnis consuetudo reddatur super amicitiam Dei ad matrem ecclesiam cui adiacet.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-q">And all church dues shall be rendered, for love of God, to the mother-church to which they belong.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und jeden Schoss zahle man um Gottes willen an die alte Pfarrkirche, der [man] zugehört.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let every customary due be paid, for the love of God, to the mother church to which [one] belongs.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares II Eg 2.2.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
